# Creator Hub — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is git-ignored.

# --- Public (safe to expose to the browser) ---------------------------------
# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Anon / public key. On newer projects this is labelled the "publishable" key
# (sb_publishable_...); either the legacy anon JWT or the new key works here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Absolute base URL of this app — used to build the private address-completion
# link (/complete/<token>). Dev defaults to http://localhost:3001 when unset;
# in production it MUST be set and MUST NOT be localhost.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://hub.example.com

# --- Server only (NEVER expose to the browser) -----------------------------
# Required ONLY to run the RLS isolation test (tests/rls.test.ts) and admin
# scripts. Do not import this anywhere in `src/`.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- IA / Creator analysis (server only) ----------------------------------
# Both must be set for the "Analisar creator" feature. The CRM works without
# them. Never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for these — the key must never reach the browser.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# Only for identity-linked API keys (org with workspaces): the wrkspc_... id.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=

# --- Support assistant (server only) -------------------------------------
# The in-app help assistant (Phase 6B) runs on its OWN model, decoupled from
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL so its cost/quality can be tuned without touching Creator
# Score. Shares ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. When unset, the assistant degrades to
# "falar com suporte" and never blocks the app. Support never spends Creator
# Score credits.
# ANTHROPIC_SUPPORT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# --- Legal (optional in dev, REQUIRED in production) -------------------------
# URLs to the reviewed Terms of Service / Privacy Policy. When set, they appear
# as links in the footer of public pages (submission form, address page). The
# CONTENT is a legal responsibility — this app only links to what you configure.
# Must be http(s); javascript:/data: are rejected.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://example.com/terms
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=https://example.com/privacy

# --- Error monitoring (optional; recommended before go-live) ----------------
# Sentry is wired but inert until a DSN is present. Server DSN is not public;
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is the browser one (can be the same project's DSN).
# Create the project manually in Sentry — see docs/production-readiness.md.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.05
# Source-map upload at build time (CI only) — needs an auth token:
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_RELEASE=            # e.g. the git SHA, for release tagging
# The /api/debug-sentry test route is 404 in production unless this is "1".
# Turn it on only while verifying the pipeline, then remove it.
# ENABLE_SENTRY_DEBUG_ROUTE=1

# --- Knowledge base seed (server only; scripts) ----------------------------
# The seed script (scripts/seed-help-articles.mjs) needs the service role key
# and the Supabase URL. It is idempotent (upsert by slug).
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=  (already listed above)
